"video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": {"file_name": "CoverLandscape.png", "id": "1279312729273224", "uri": "https://scontent-iad6-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/39031422_1279312735939890_4968861642343199335_n.png?_nc_cat=109&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=b5hYaQ6wjkoQ7kNvwGGVmZ2&_nc_oc=AdoqQz4R0tUzrzrM3nbTdJnCvasS2UK1OGzaKfF27krhPlOb7Ms1EG4XvWX-Usvl7hw&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad6-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQTmFd-YALtIAYXS1FI40VNC8TaP4uZ3ukkUIKcvbghIdg&oe=6AF5CF22"}, "display_name": "3D scan of a basalt canyon", "keywords": [], "long_description": "Move like a pedestrian in a basalt canyon, reconstructed from videos taken by a helmet-held 360 camera, whose trajectory is about 800m long.\n\nRight controller:\n- Rotate on the left or right by using the joystick\n- Update the vertical offset (up or down) by using the joystick\n- Choose a location and teleport to it by using the virtual laser pointer\n- Teleport by using the index trigger only if the laser is green (not red)\n\nLeft controller:\n- Move continuously by using the joystick\n- Switch pannel and map by using the grip/hand trigger\n- If both map and pannel are disabled, switch between rendering modes (texturing or normal colors) by pressing the index trigger\n- The map shows the cloud of mesh vertices and the user location\n- If the pannel is enabled, switch between constrained and unconstrained motions by pressing the index trigger\n- The constrained motion controls your height above the ground\n- The pannel shows information about the 3D model and the selected motion.\n", "short_description": "Move continuously like a pedestrian in a basalt canyon, which was computed by photogrammetry from a cubemap video (4096x1344x2) taken by a helmet-held 360 camera (Gopro Max) and by walking about 800 meters.\n"}]}, "developer_name": "Maxime Lhuillier", "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://maximelhuillier.fr/", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "Unity 2019.4", "support_we